# Admin Web Portal

Next.js App Router project for internal operations and back-office workflows.

## Product knowledge wiki

Follow the wiki workflow in the workspace root `AGENTS.md` before implementing a feature:
the feature must be in `ready-for-dev` or `in-dev` with `advisory-review` not `pending`, and it
must have a wiki page. For this app, read:

- `knowledge/wiki/app-requirements/[feature-id]-web-admin-portal.md` for admin portal-specific implementation requirements
- `knowledge/wiki/design/[feature-id]-[slug].md` for UI design decisions

This slice has this structure:

- `/admin` route space with protected dashboard pages
- credentials-first auth for operators
- management tables and workflow-oriented screens
- a same-origin `/api/v1/*` proxy for backend calls; it forwards only plain paths under `/api/v1/`
- sign-out through `signOutEverywhere` (`lib/auth/sign-out.ts`), which revokes the backend refresh session before Auth.js clears the web session
- no hosting configuration; the `deployment` skill holds worked examples

## Focus Areas

- Keep this slice operational and staff-facing.
- Prefer dashboards, tables, filters, and action modals over marketing components.
- Treat role checks and audit visibility as first-class requirements.
- Keep backend integration centralized through shared API helpers and route handlers.
